Original commit body from 682778ef1fb47ae413d1491ce1225b120ec7b871:

The vendor-attribution scrub was a commit-msg hook and nothing else, so it
protected exactly one channel. A PR title, a PR body and a PR comment are
none of those, and all three reached the forge unscrubbed. Found when a
merged PR body was observed carrying a vendor session URL on its last line.

Nothing was wrong with the matching. The shipped pattern list matches that
URL correctly (both word boundaries are supplied by the '/' and the '.'),
and the line sat at the end of the body, inside the scan window that already
exists. The rule was simply enforced at one of six egress points, because it
lived inside the hook that discovered it first.

So the matcher, the phrase selection and the line sweep move to
.githooks/brand-scrub.sh, which lib/forgejo-api.sh sources -- that one line
is what makes a single pattern list govern every publisher. commit-msg is
refactored onto the same library rather than keeping a second copy; what
stays in the hook is what is genuinely specific to a commit message.

Policy is unchanged and deliberately so: delete body lines, substitute
titles, keep the first/last-10-line window. Refusing instead was considered
and declined -- PR bodies here are fulsome, so losing a few words costs less
than handing a human a blocked PR, and the pattern list is full of ordinary
English (falcon is a framework this project ships support for).

scripts/check-forge-text-egress is the backstop. There is no single choke
point to defend -- auto-pr alone emits a body at three points, because
'git push -o' cannot carry newlines -- so every api_post / api_patch /
-o description= site must declare '# forge-egress: scrubbed' or
'# forge-egress: no-agent-text -- <reason>'. A planted undeclared site
proves the linter is not vacuous.

Three defects found while building it, each now pinned by a regression test
that uses the caller's real shape rather than a convenient one:

  - The reporter read a count set inside '$(...)', a subshell, so it was
    unbound in the parent under set -u. It now re-sweeps the before-text,
    which is also exact: diffing line counts over-reported, because command
    substitution strips the trailing newline the sweep leaves behind.
  - bs_init read $HOME eagerly, so sourcing the library aborted in any
    environment without one. The auto-pr suite runs with a minimal env
    precisely to reproduce the caller's shell, and caught it. The key is
    lazy now, and only phrase selection ever needs it.
  - auto-pr discarded every stderr write from its lock line onward:
    'exec {FD}>>"$f" 2>/dev/null' makes BOTH redirections permanent. That
    is what made the two above surface as exit 1 with no output at all.
    Scoping the exec to a brace group keeps the descriptor and restores
    stderr. Filed separately; the other two exec-redirect sites in the tree
    redirect no standard stream.

Verified end to end rather than by proxy: a real auto-pr run whose
description ended in a vendor URL queued the prose with the URL gone, the
title intact, exit 0, and 'removed 1 line(s)' on stderr. 1795 python tests
and 59 hook tests green, mypy ratchet clean.

